  "id": "video_edit_ltx2_5_iclora_union_control",
  "name": "LTX 2.5 IC-LoRA — video to video (depth control + audio)",
  "description": "Restyle a video while keeping its motion and 3D layout. Upload a source video (and, optionally, a start image): a depth map is extracted from every frame (Video Depth Anything) and used as a guide, so LTX 2.5 generates a new video that moves like the original — in the style of your prompt and start image — with a freshly generated soundtrack (the original audio is not kept).\n\nThe start image becomes the opening frame; a restyled still of your video's first frame works best. Untick \"Use a start image\" to let the prompt alone set the look — then no image is needed. \"Enhance prompt with AI\" lets a small Gemma model rewrite your prompt into a fuller description first. Lower \"Control strength\" to let the result drift further from the source's structure.\n\nOnly the start of your clip is used (\"Clip length used\", default 5 s), at its own frame rate and aspect ratio. The video is rendered in two passes, a fast 8-step pass at the working resolution and then a 2× upscale pass, so a working resolution of 512 gives a 1024p result. Clip length and resolution drive the time.",
  "category": "video-edit",
  "tags": [
    "ltx",
    "ltx2.5",
    "ic-lora",
    "union-control",
    "vid2vid",
    "depth",
    "distilled",
    "video",
    "audio"
  ],
  "promptGuides": [
    {
      "label": "LTX union control (depth / canny / pose) — Lightricks",
      "url": "https://docs.ltx.io/open-source-model/feature-guides/structural-control/union-control",
      "tip": "Describe the look you want — style, materials, characters, lighting, sound — not the motion or the control map: the movement comes from your video."
    },
    {
      "label": "LTX prompting guide",
      "url": "https://docs.ltx.io/open-source-model/usage-guides/prompting-guide"
    }
